From f54c2bd22708d1a32246a06a6ca418b6e024eb3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Struan Bartlett <struan.bartlett@NewsNow.co.uk>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:22:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] passthrough: Set FOPEN_NOFLUSH on files opened read-only

The guest kernel sends FUSE_FLUSH on every close() of a FUSE file, and
the close() waits for the reply.  virtiofsd answers it by dup()ing and
closing the host descriptor, which matters only for a descriptor that
can write (to pass on write-back errors from the host file system on
close) or that holds POSIX locks.  virtiofsd does not implement POSIX
or BSD locks (the guest kernel handles them locally), so for a file
opened O_RDONLY the FLUSH round trip achieves nothing.

Set FOPEN_NOFLUSH in the OPEN reply for such files, so that the guest
skips it.  Workloads that open and read many small files, such as a
shell running scripts, a compiler reading headers, or `cat` and
`grep` over a tree, save one synchronous round trip per file.

Kernels older than 5.16 ignore the flag, and the guest kernel ignores
it when writeback caching is on, so behaviour is unchanged there.
Files opened for writing still get FLUSH as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/passthrough/mod.rs | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/passthrough/mod.rs b/src/passthrough/mod.rs
index d0712d3..ad5e912 100644
--- a/src/passthrough/mod.rs
+++ b/src/passthrough/mod.rs
@@ -987,6 +987,16 @@ impl PassthroughFs {
             _ => {}
         };
 
+        // `flush()` only dup()s and closes the host file descriptor, to pass on the guest's
+        // close() to the host file system.  For a descriptor without write access, that has no
+        // observable effect: there is no data to write back, and we do not support POSIX locks
+        // (the guest kernel handles them locally), so no host lock can be released by it.  Tell
+        // the guest it need not send FUSE_FLUSH on every close() of such a file.  (The guest
+        // ignores this when writeback caching is enabled.)
+        if flags & (libc::O_ACCMODE as u32) == libc::O_RDONLY as u32 {
+            opts |= OpenOptions::NOFLUSH;
+        }
+
         Ok((Some(handle), opts))
     }
 
